<title>USA: EA Industries Q4 Dec 31 Q4 shr loss $3.07.</title>
<headline>EA Industries Q4 Dec 31 Q4 shr loss $3.07.</headline>
<dateline>WEST LONG BRANCH, N.J. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 loss $  3.07	   loss $  1.08</p>
<p> Net		 loss  16,188	   loss   4,026</p>
<p> Net sales		 17,617		   20,956</p>
<p> Avg shrs	     5,272,874		3,743,684</p>
<p>12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 loss $  6.24	   loss $ 10.01</p>
<p> Net		 loss  29,954	   loss  30,894</p>
<p> Revs			81,625		   77,085</p>
<p> Avg shrs	     4,802,068		3,086,070</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers) NOTES:</p>
<p>1.  Net loss for 1966 included charges of $5.8 million related tdo the termination of merger discussion with Aydin Corp. The loss also included charges totalling $2.6 million and $2.5 million related to the company's BarOn investment and joint venture with Israel Aircraft Industries, respectively. The company also recorded a charge to expense of $4.2 million resulting from issuance of convertible debt. The net loss for 1995 included a charge to purchased research and development of $19.6 million. 2.  Share and per share amounts have been adjusted to give retroactive effect to a one-for-four reverse stock split as of December 27, 1996.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
